    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP\u2019s June 23 slate, our premier offensive pillars are anchored by **Mickey Moniak** (74.73) and **Josh Naylor** (72.86). **Mickey Moniak** is our highest-rated play, buoyed by an exceptional park environment and a favorable platoon matchup against Gray, while **Josh Naylor** benefits significantly from a high-efficiency matchup against Keller and wind conditions shifting in his favor. **Corbin Carroll** (72.25) remains a must-start, providing a necessary injection of SB upside against Leahy despite a modest park penalty. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** continues to provide high-floor value, as his position in the #2 hole and solid contact profile overcome the daunting task of facing a tough southpaw in Lodolo.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench with a 51.70 score. While **Zach McKinstry** offered a respectable platoon advantage, the depth of our middle infield and the higher ceiling of **Alex Freeland**\u2014whose 56.66 score is driven by a favorable matchup against the lower-tier Rojas\u2014pushed him to the pine to maximize our daily efficiency. We are also monitoring \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Max Muncy**, **Austin Riley**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Henry Bolte**. While these hitters are projected into favorable spots\u2014specifically the wind advantage for the trio facing the lefty Robbie Ray\u2014the lack of official lineups adds a layer of variance to their projected outputs. Finally, **James Wood** bears watching; despite a 54.86 score, his utility is hampered by a significant -14% penalty against a high-skill arm like Luzardo and an elite catcher who threatens his SB production, requiring close observation as the game approaches.",
